# Bonewalker — the sixth .blob character authored from scratch, and the first
# authored WITH `blob:rings` as the primary instrument (trial of the tool).
# Reference: docs/dev-notes/refs/bonewalker-mesh/bonewalker.glb — a Meshy
# "Rusted Bonewalker": a horned, skeletal undead biped, 1.700 m in its own
# bind T-pose, authored here at 1.30 m (scale 0.7647). 67% of its vertices
# reach a measurable bone (mouse 40%, schoolgirl 79%).
#
# WHAT IT IS (seen in Blender renders of the mesh, 2026-08-27): a grinning
# skull with two thick horns sweeping out-then-up from the temples, pale
# eyes, a wide mouth with blocky teeth; exposed segmented vertebrae down the
# whole back; ribcage and pelvis bones showing through rusted red-brown
# meat; bony shoulder shrugs; thin arms with long pale claw fingers; short
# paw feet with pale claws, splayed wide. Skin = dark rusted red-brown
# (texture mode sRGB 84,40,26), bone = pale dust (brightest texels sRGB
# 175,140,119). The mesh material also carries its own texture as an
# EMISSIVE map, which is why Blender renders read brighter than the raw
# albedo.
#
# MEASURED SKELETON — every len= below is the reference rig's own
# joint-to-joint distance x 0.7647 (the .l bones; .r differs by <3%):
#   pelvis 0.092 (7.1%)  spine1 0.092  chest 0.092  spine2 0.050 (3.9%)
#   neck 0.068 (5.2%)  clavicle 0.111 (8.6%)  upperarm 0.257 (19.8%)
#   forearm 0.213 (16.4%)  thigh 0.289 (22.3%)  shin 0.329 (25.3%)
#   foot 0.126 (9.7%).  Legs (thigh+shin) are 47.6% of standing height and
# the forearms are long — a lanky skeletal build. DO NOT correct these
# toward human proportions; blob:rings flags any drift over ~10%.
#
# THE RIG-vs-SURFACE OFFSET (why this skeleton is shaped the way it is):
# the Meshy rig puts its Hips joint at 58.1% of height (0.755 m scaled) —
# high in the pelvis — while the hip sockets sit at 53% and the SURFACE
# crotch at 49.7% (0.646 m). Chaining straight measured-length legs
# (0.289+0.329) from the rig's own Hips would leave the feet 11 cm off the
# floor, so the pelvis root sits at the surface crotch 0.646 and the whole
# spine chain rides ~0.108 below the rig's joints. Consequences:
#   - the clavicle parents to NECK (tail 1.040 = the mesh's shoulder
#     surface line, T-pose arm axis 1.052), not to chest (tail 0.922 —
#     13 cm below the shoulder line);
#   - the skull bone is deliberately LONG (0.362): the face block rides
#     skull at=0.45 (fixed in face.ts), so 1.040 + 0.45*0.362 = 1.203 puts
#     the cranium centre midway between the measured chin (1.106) and
#     crown (1.300). The skull bone is unmapped (ref-align.ts) — no fit
#     sees its length; the head prims and face block are what it positions.
#
# The reference stands T-posed with legs in a slight crouch (knee +0.077
# forward of the hip, ankle swung back); this file rests the arms down at a
# natural angle and keeps a mild knee bend — blob:rings is pose-independent
# per bone, so the T-pose arms do not pollute the fit; blob:measure WILL
# print POSE MISMATCH on the whole figure (score leg windows instead).
model bonewalker
  height 1.30
  # Checked, not decorative — see blob-checks.ts.
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # ROOT: head at the surface crotch (0.646 = 49.7% of the mesh), tail at
  # the hip line 0.738 — straight measured legs land the ankle at 0.129,
  # matching the mesh's 0.117-0.131 foot band.
  root pelvis at 0.646 len=0.092
  # Spine chain: measured lengths, slight forward pitch (the rig rises
  # z -0.026 -> -0.000 over the spine — a small forward lean; +z is front).
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=2 len=0.092   # tail 0.830 = the mesh's waist pinch (0.825)
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=2 len=0.092   # ribcage
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=1 len=0.050
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=0 len=0.068   # tail 1.040 = shoulder/neck-base line
  # LONG ON PURPOSE — see the header: carries the face block up to cranium
  # centre 1.203 (chin 1.106, crown 1.300).
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=0 len=0.362

  mirror
    # Clavicle on the NECK (not chest) so the shoulder ball sits at the
    # mesh's shoulder line: head (0.030, 1.040), tail x 0.141 — the rig's
    # own Arm joint is at x 0.140 scaled.
    bone clavicle parent=neck    side=0.030 dir=side len=0.111
    # Arms rest DOWN (the mesh T-poses) — lanky measured lengths left as
    # measured. Wrist ends at y ~0.57, claws to ~0.47: past the crotch,
    # which is what 19.8%+16.4% arms on a 1.30 m frame give.
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=8 pitch=4  len=0.257
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=4 pitch=12 len=0.213
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down tilt=2 pitch=10 len=0.095
    # Legs: measured lengths; mild crouch from the mesh stance (knee
    # forward, ankle back) and a wide splay (mesh ankles x +/-0.17-0.23).
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down tilt=10 pitch=10 side=0.085 len=0.289
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=-2 pitch=-10          len=0.329
    # The foot bone only positions paw prims (house pattern — mouse.blob).
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                              len=0.126
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — a meat-starved frame: hip wings (pelvis halfW ~0.090-0.119),
  # a genuine wasp waist (33-40mm half-width at y 0.825, measured on the
  # Hips/Spine02 vertex clouds), then a ribcage DEEPER than wide (halfD
  # 0.121 vs halfW 0.109 at y 0.950). The pale-bone mottle + the painted
  # spine ridge carry the "rusted meat over bone" read.
  # ============================================================
  # Pelvis/hip bowl: y 0.646-0.75, halfW ~0.10-0.115 (the iliac flare),
  # halfD ~0.075-0.090.
  # Pelvis/hip bowl: y 0.646-0.75. blob:rings block 2 asked r 0.080->0.054
  # / wide 1.40->1.19 (semi-axis 64mm) and the applied result STARVED the
  # hips on screen — the mesh's own width profile is 75-90mm halfW at
  # y 0.65-0.675 (119mm at the iliac flare), and the fit's t 0-0.59 support
  # cannot see the wings (they are the off-ends it dropped). Split the
  # difference at the measured profile: halfW 0.090.
  blob torso on pelvis  at=0.45 r=0.060 wide=1.28 tall=1.15 deep=1.00 blend=0.011 offset=(0,0,-0.0028)
  # HIP WINGS: the fit reads the bowl MASS (~55-65mm rho; it asked three
  # rounds for ~52mm semi-axis) but the mesh's iliac crests are BLADES
  # spiking to 90-119mm halfW — a radial blob cannot express a blade, so
  # the wings get their own two prims. World-measured, not fit-measured.
  blob torso on pelvis  at=0.62 offset=(0.078,0.012,-0.010) r=0.030 wide=0.75 tall=0.90 deep=1.10 blend=0.008 both
  # Waist -> ribcage (spine1 0.738-0.830). blob:rings block 3 (mean 31.8mm,
  # 43% blend-dominated): the waist is a PINCH between the pelvis cap and
  # the ribcage cap, not a column — r 0.0243/r2 0.0191 with the smin of the
  # neighbours is what the field measures. deep 0.92: slightly shallower
  # than wide front-to-back.
  bar  torso on spine1  from=0.02 to=1.00 r=0.0243 r2=0.0191 deep=0.92 offset=(0,0,-0.0086) blend=0.010
  # Ribcage (chest 0.830-0.922). blob:rings block 4 round 2 asked r ~0.09
  # forward of centre (offset z +0.0215 — the mesh front z +0.110 at y 0.95
  # vs back -0.08 under the spine ridge). from=0.60: a capsule's bottom cap
  # is a half-radius hemisphere, so a bar starting at the bone head filled
  # the waist pinch at 0.825 (the pin caught it: 80mm where the mesh is
  # 33-40). The bar owns the flare 0.885-0.950; the girdle blob carries the
  # max band (mesh 106-109mm halfW at 0.925-0.95).
  bar  torso on chest   from=0.60 to=1.30 r=0.085 r2=0.070 deep=1.13 offset=(0,0,0.0215) blend=0.012
  # Upper chest / shoulder girdle base (spine2 0.922-0.972 + the trap
  # region the clavicle cloud carries): caps the ribcage at its widest
  # (y ~0.95-1.00) and shrugs up toward the neck base. wide 1.75 keeps its
  # surface at x ~0.080 at the shoulder-ball height (1.04) so the balls
  # fuse — the fuse probe needs real contact, not near-miss (goblin lesson).
  blob torso on spine2  at=0.40 r=0.060 wide=1.95 tall=1.30 deep=1.10 blend=0.010
  # TRAPS: the mesh shrugs — bony traps rise from the neck base to the
  # shoulder balls (clavicle cloud rho peaks 0.090-0.108 near the neck).
  # Also what welds the raised shoulder balls (offset up+back per blob:rings
  # block 6) to the torso — the fuse probe needs real contact.
  blob torso on spine2  at=0.70 offset=(0.055,0.045,-0.012) r=0.042 wide=1.10 tall=0.95 deep=0.95 blend=0.008 both

  # Bony neck: short and thin (mesh ~0.030-0.040 half-width at y 1.04-1.08);
  # runs up into the jaw and down into the shoulder mass to fuse head->torso.
  bar head on neck from=-0.4 to=1.6 r=0.032 deep=1.44 offset=(0,0,-0.0171) blend=0.005

  # ============================================================
  # EXPOSED SPINE — the character's signature. The mesh runs segmented
  # vertebrae down the whole back (backmost surface z -0.080 sacrum to
  # -0.121 mid-back, vs the torso's own back plane ~0.025-0.04 shallower).
  # One painted bone bar per spine bone, offset to sit clearly PROUD of the
  # back surface (v1's -0.058/-0.062 vanished inside the torso's own back
  # plane — the render showed no ridge from behind; the mesh's ridge is the
  # BACKMOST feature, z -0.080 sacrum to -0.121 mid-back). Plus groove cuts
  # for the segmentation. BONE paint — the paint boundary is the prim
  # boundary.
  # ============================================================
  bar torso on pelvis  from=0.35 to=1.00 offset=(0,0,-0.075) r=0.024 r2=0.027 blend=0.006 color=dbc0a0
  bar torso on spine1  from=0.05 to=0.95 offset=(0,0,-0.080) r=0.026 r2=0.029 blend=0.006 color=dbc0a0
  bar torso on chest   from=0.10 to=1.60 offset=(0,0,-0.085) r=0.028 r2=0.031 blend=0.006 color=dbc0a0
  # The ridge continues up the upper back to the neck base — the mesh's
  # thoracic vertebrae run to y ~1.04 (its upper-spine ridge verts are
  # claimed by the clavicle cloud there). Without this segment the back
  # plane at 0.95-1.04 is 45mm shallower than the mesh's.
  bar torso on spine2  from=-0.2 to=1.20 offset=(0,0,-0.072) r=0.026 r2=0.024 blend=0.006 color=dbc0a0
  # Segmentation grooves across the lumbar and thoracic ridge.
  groove torso on spine1 at=0.50 offset=(0,0,-0.070) r=0.030 wide=1.6 tall=0.10 depth=0.004 width=0.005
  groove torso on chest  at=0.45 offset=(0,0,-0.075) r=0.032 wide=1.6 tall=0.10 depth=0.004 width=0.005

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD — the cranium + jaw ride the face block (centre 1.203, crown
  # 1.300, chin 1.106 — all measured off the Head-vertex cloud). The
  # horns are the measured 0.286-wide feature at y 1.215-1.26; the mouth
  # and eyes come from the baked face decal (sheet block below).
  # ============================================================
  # HORNS: bases at the skull's top-sides (x +/-0.048, y ~1.21), sweeping
  # out to x +/-0.103 + r 0.024 = 0.127 (mesh 0.143) and up to y ~1.29,
  # curling forward. Bend x pushes the belly outward; `both` mirrors the
  # sweep so the pair curls symmetrically.
  bar head on skull from=0.27 to=0.33 offset=(0.048,0.062,-0.005) tip=(0.070,0.075,0.014) bend=(0.050,0.012,0.0) r=0.024 r2=0.007 blend=0.004 chamfer both color=dbc0a0
  # Small pointed ears under the horn bases (the head cloud is 56-63mm
  # half-wide at y 1.17-1.20 vs the 52mm cranium — only ~10mm of ear
  # protrudes; v1's 0.014+0.020tip rendered as bat wings). PAINTED flesh:
  # unpainted, they sit within the face decal's reach and picked up the
  # bake's horn-cream pixels.
  blob head on skull at=0.30 offset=(0.056,0.022,0.002) tip=(0.010,0.010,-0.004) r=0.009 r2=0.003 blend=0.003 chamfer both color=693b2b

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS — skeletal thin (measured shaft rho 0.023-0.030 vs schoolgirl's
  # 0.026 thigh-thin arms on a smaller frame). Shoulder ball is the arm's
  # core (house pattern). The hand is a bony mitt + four pale claw
  # fingers (the rig ends at one Hand joint — no finger attribution is
  # possible; claws authored by eye off the renders).
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on clavicle at=0.80 r=0.046 blend=0.007 mirror core offset=(0,0.0206,-0.0233)
  # Upperarm: blob:rings block 9 — fatter at the shoulder (0.0346), thinner
  # at the elbow (0.0181); the mesh deltoid carries real mass.
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.03 to=0.97 r=0.0383 r2=0.0162 wide=1.098 offset=(0,0,-0.0035) blend=0.005 mirror
  blob arm on forearm  at=0.00 r=0.029 blend=0.005 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.05 to=0.95 r=0.0333 r2=0.0212 deep=1.114 offset=(0,0,0.0086) blend=0.005 mirror
  # Bony palm, slightly deep (the mesh hand is 0.111 long for ~0.09 width).
  blob arm on hand     at=0.30 r=0.026 wide=0.90 tall=1.15 deep=1.30 blend=0.004 mirror
  # Four claw fingers fanning off the palm, pale bone, tapering to points.
  # Splay via distinct x offsets; each tip curls slightly forward (+z) and
  # inward — a relaxed raking hand. ~0.012 apart at 0.008 radius.
  bar arm on hand from=0.45 to=1.40 offset=(0.016,0,-0.004) tip=(0.010,0,0.028) r=0.009 r2=0.003 blend=0.0025 mirror color=dbc0a0
  bar arm on hand from=0.50 to=1.45 offset=(0.005,0,-0.002) tip=(0.003,0,0.030) r=0.009 r2=0.003 blend=0.0025 mirror color=dbc0a0
  bar arm on hand from=0.50 to=1.40 offset=(-0.006,0,-0.001) tip=(-0.004,0,0.029) r=0.008 r2=0.003 blend=0.0025 mirror color=dbc0a0
  bar arm on hand from=0.45 to=1.30 offset=(-0.016,0,0.002) tip=(-0.011,0,0.025) r=0.008 r2=0.002 blend=0.0025 mirror color=dbc0a0

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS — thin thighs (rho 0.032-0.054), knees that KNOB (the mesh shows
  # bony knee balls), calves that bulge BACK (shin cloud rho 0.058-0.065
  # mid-shin, the bulge in +z/-z), ankles tapering to 0.034. Paw feet
  # with pale claws, splayed outward like the mesh (toes to x +/-0.286).
  # ============================================================
  blob leg on thigh at=0.00 r=0.055 blend=0.007 mirror core
  # Thigh: blob:rings block 10 — slimmer and narrower side-to-side than v1
  # (r 0.0399, wide 0.836), knee-end 0.0383; sits 12mm forward of the bone
  # (the mesh thigh mass hangs forward of the femur line). Taper REFUSED
  # (the profile bends: hip ball -> shaft -> knee), so no r2 story — the
  # knee blob and the profile carry it.
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.08 to=0.96 r=0.0458 r2=0.0367 wide=0.836 deep=0.999 offset=(0,0,0.0122) blend=0.006 mirror
  # Knee knob.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.00 r=0.042 deep=0.95 blend=0.006 mirror
  # Calf: blob:rings block 5 — narrower side-to-side (wide 0.77), the bulge
  # is front-to-back (r2 0.0645 deep).
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.10 to=0.55 r=0.0383 r2=0.0645 wide=0.77 deep=1.10 offset=(0,0,-0.0099) blend=0.006 mirror
  # Calf -> ankle taper: block 7 — narrow (0.777) and slightly deep (1.053),
  # 7.5mm back; round 3 thinned the ankle end to r2 0.0403.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.55 to=0.97 r=0.0246 r2=0.0403 wide=0.777 deep=1.053 offset=(0,0,-0.0075) blend=0.006 mirror
  # PAW: a short deep mass under the ankle (ankle 0.129, sole 0.00),
  # yawed slightly out (mesh feet splay; toes reach x +/-0.286).
  blob leg on foot  at=0.10 offset=(0.018,-0.062,0.020) r=0.048 wide=1.10 tall=1.30 deep=1.40 blend=0.006 mirror
  # Three toe claws per paw, pale bone, splayed in x, reaching forward-down.
  blob leg on foot  at=0.0 offset=(0.052,-0.070,0.095) tip=(0.016,-0.045,0.050) r=0.017 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 mirror color=dbc0a0
  blob leg on foot  at=0.0 offset=(0.014,-0.075,0.105) tip=(0.004,-0.048,0.055) r=0.018 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 mirror color=dbc0a0
  blob leg on foot  at=0.0 offset=(-0.026,-0.070,0.095) tip=(-0.010,-0.045,0.048) r=0.016 r2=0.004 blend=0.003 mirror color=dbc0a0

# ============================================================
# FACE — cranium measured off the Head cloud: halfW 0.052-0.063, back
# z -0.054, face front +0.118 (the teeth row); chin 1.106, crown 1.300,
# centre 1.203. The mouth/eyes are the BAKED DECAL (sheet block) — the
# skill is emphatic that agents cannot paint faces from prims.
# ============================================================
face
  # Cranium: r 0.066 with these scales gives half (0.061, 0.094, 0.099) —
  # deep, because the mesh face front (+0.118) is far forward of the
  # skull's back (-0.054) and the teeth row IS the front surface.
  headRadius 0.066
  headWidth  0.92
  headHeight 1.42
  headDepth  1.50
  jawWidth   0.82
  jawHeight  0.72
  jawDrop    0.085
  # The chin/jaw juts: the mesh jaw front (z +0.106 at y 1.095) is as far
  # forward as the face — an undershot skull jaw.
  jawJut     0.055
  # Brow ridge is prominent on the mesh (bony shelf over the eyes).
  noseLength 0.006
  noseWidth  0.50
  noseDrop   0.030
  browHeavy  0.011
  browRise   0.030
  headBlend  0.005

# Face decal: `npm run blob:face-bake -- bonewalker` baked the mesh's own
# head (top 16.5%: horned skull, head box 0.475 wide x 0.280 tall — the
# horns make the box wide). Projection aimed at TWO features in head space
# of the fattest head prim (the face block's cranium, centre (0,1.203),
# semi-axes 0.061x0.094x0.099): the image's eye row (uv.y 0.64) at hs.y
# +0.208, and the image's bony CHIN row (uv.y 0.32) at hs.y -0.85 — that
# pair puts the teeth between them (uv.y 0.40 at hs.y -0.59, y 1.148) and
# keeps the jaw's bottom (hs.y -1.03) on the image's chin-shadow rows
# instead of the naked dark band the first aim (eyes+teeth) left there.
# scaleY 0.302, centreY 0.577. scaleX 0.125 maps the image's eye gap
# (uv.x 0.42/0.58) onto hs.x +/-0.63 = x +/-0.038 (wide-set eyes); the
# horn imagery lives at uv.x < 0.2 / > 0.8, past the cranium and the decal
# clamp, so it never smears onto the skull.
sheet
  image       bonewalker-face.png
  decal       1
  projScaleX  0.125
  projScaleY  0.302
  projCentreX 0.5
  projCentreY 0.577

# Palette measured off the embedded texture (2026-08-27): dominant mode
# sRGB (84,40,26) dark rusted red-brown -> linear (0.089,0.021,0.011),
# lifted ~1.7x because the lab key is strong and the mottle averages the
# mean toward the bone dust. Bone mottle = the brightest texel band
# sRGB (175,140,119) -> linear (0.44,0.26,0.19), brightened toward the
# painted-prim bone dbc0a0 (linear 0.68,0.53,0.37) so meat and bone read
# as one family. Mottle differs in HUE (grey-gold over red), not just
# value — the "bone showing through meat" look is the whole character.
palette
  baseColor     0.155 0.050 0.028
  deepColor     0.28 0.05 0.05
  charColor     0.20 0.08 0.05
  specIntensity 0.50
  specRoughness 0.42
  fresnelBoost  0.35
  translucency  0.18
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.25
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.0
  wetness       0.15
  mottleAmp     0.38
  mottleScale   1.6
  mottleColor   0.46 0.38 0.31
